# E33 -- Can placement alone keep a water layer alive? LAKE, only the water layer managed and rotation enabled, groups and ecology off. The placed arm tops the map up to twelve feature-layer wild animals every 5,000 ticks, drawing only from water entries that are stocked and in season, through the tool's own headless placement (addendum 47: dfhack.units.create plus a population reference, no menu and no pointer). The control arm places nothing and only counts. One season, 100,800 ticks, two replicates each. E20 is the wider control: a full year of the same roster with no placement gave zero water arrivals and an empty layer by midsummer.
run 20260918-082312 fort LAKE backup LAKE.preverify
DF v0.53.16 win64 STEAM DFHack 53.16-r1.1 world The Domain of Winds site 48 tiles 12..13,28..28 seed 424242
commits: DwarfCron 59050eb seasonal-wildlife d478515 fps cap 1000

## Predictions (written before the run)
- placement holds the layer: the placed arm sits at or near twelve water animals for the whole season while the control falls toward zero; the entries debit by roughly the number placed; no citizen dies of it
- placed animals do not persist: the placed count falls back between top-ups faster than countdowns explain, or placed units vanish from the active list
- placement fights the game: a Lua error, a stalled tick, a save that is no longer byte-identical, or placed units drowning or beaching

